      "code": "# pick up cube and place on green target marker, then let go\n\nobj = get_object()\ntarget = get_target()\n\nobj_pos = obj['pos']\nobj_half = obj['half_height']\n\n# Approach just above the object's centre so that, when the gripper closes,\n# the fingertips contact the top face of the cube.\n# Object centre z = 0.2799, top face at 0.3049; we set grasp point at 0.2859\n# (\u22486\u202fmm above centre, well below the top surface).\napproach_z = obj_pos[2] + 0.006\napproach_pos = [obj_pos[0], obj_pos[1], approach_z]\n\n# Open the gripper fully before moving in.\nopen_gripper()\n\n# Move the grasp point to the position just above the cube.\nmove_to(approach_pos, quat=None, timeout=4.0)\n\n# Close the gripper to grasp the cube.\nclose_gripper()\n\n# Lift the cube a small distance.\nlift(dz=0.1, timeout=4.0)\n\n# Move to the target marker, stopping a little above the table top (z = 0.255).\ntarget_pos = target['pos']\nrelease_z = 0.255 + 0.02   # 2\u202fcm above table surface\nrelease_pos = [target_pos[0], target_pos[1], release_z]\nmove_to(release_pos, quat=None, timeout=4.0)\n\n# Open the gripper to release the cube onto the table.\nopen_gripper()\n\n# Let the simulation settle.\nwait(0.5)",
