      "code": "obj = get_object()\ntgt = get_target()\n\n# Start with the gripper fully open\nopen_gripper()\n\n# --- Grasp the object from above ---\n# 1. Move to a safe height directly above the object\nabove_obj = [obj['pos'][0], obj['pos'][1], obj['pos'][2] + obj['half_height'] + 0.1]\nmove_to(above_obj)\n\n# 2. Descend so the fingertips touch the top of the object.\n#    The fingertip point is 2\u202fcm below the pad top; placing the grasp point\n#    2\u202fcm below the object\u2019s top puts the pad top at the object surface.\ncontact_obj = [obj['pos'][0], obj['pos'][1], obj['pos'][2] + obj['half_height'] - 0.02]\nmove_to(contact_obj)\n\n# 3. Close the gripper to grasp the object\nclose_gripper()\n\n# 4. Lift the object clear of the table\nlift(0.2)\n\n# --- Place the object on the target marker ---\n# 5. Move to a safe height directly above the target marker\nabove_tgt = [tgt['pos'][0], tgt['pos'][1], tgt['pos'][2] + obj['half_height'] + 0.1]\nmove_to(above_tgt)\n\n# 6. Lower the object so its top is at the target marker height\ntarget_contact = [tgt['pos'][0], tgt['pos'][1], tgt['pos'][2] + obj['half_height']]\nmove_to(target_contact)\n\n# 7. Release the object\nopen_gripper()\n\n# 8. Let the simulation settle\nwait(0.5)",
